# Uncle Mario - Guided First-Shift Tutorial (Hands-On, Punchy, Witty Fake-Skip)
# On-screen HelperPrompt shows exact keybinds while Uncle Mario speaks in warm, brisk Tito voice.
# Covers: Pricing (Alt/L), First Sale (Anoba), Fridge, Nokia Call, Store Upgrades (U), Events & Calendar (C).

UncleMario: Settled in behind the counter already, anak?
UncleMario: Your Lola would grin ear to ear seeing these shelves open again.
UncleMario: Ready for a quick test run before neighbors walk up?
- Show me the ropes, Uncle.
	UncleMario: Sige, hands-on is fastest!
- I've got this, Uncle!
	UncleMario: Nice try, anak! Your Lola made me swear on her good frying pan I'd test you first.
	UncleMario: Relax, it'll take less than a minute!

UncleMario: Check the shelf on your left first. Try tweaking the price on [color=#0f6e2f]Anoba[/color].
[signal arg="wait_for_price_change"]
UncleMario: Sharp! Fair prices earn extra tips, greedy markups earn complaints.
UncleMario: Speaking of [color=#0f6e2f]Anoba[/color], sell me a pack! Skipped breakfast hauling your crates.
[signal arg="wait_for_sale"]
UncleMario: Ahh, still crispy! First honest peso in your drawer, anak.
UncleMario: Next, check Lola's refrigerator on your right. Pull the handle.
[signal arg="wait_for_fridge"]
UncleMario: Keep that door shut between grabs so the cold doesn't leak out.
UncleMario: Now ring me on the Nokia behind you! That's how you order restocks.
[signal arg="wait_for_tutorial_call"]
UncleMario: Haha! Standing two feet away and my pocket still buzzed!
UncleMario: Lola's utang notebook sits right beside that phone too, in case neighbors ask for credit.
UncleMario: Quick peek at your Store Upgrades board too, anak. That's where you grow Lola's shop.
[signal arg="wait_for_upgrades"]
UncleMario: Nice, right? New stock tiers, fridge parts, Mingming, I haul all of it on my tricycle.
UncleMario: One last board! Pull up the Calendar and Events menu so market rushes never blindside you.
[signal arg="wait_for_events"]
UncleMario: Good eye! Active events, moon cards, and your day tracker all live right there.
jump SuccessOutro

label Satisfy
label SuccessOutro
UncleMario: That's the whole counter, anak! You're ready for real customers.
jump Outro

label Outro
UncleMario: Tricycle's idling outside. Ring my Nokia anytime you need a haul, ha!
[signal arg="refuse_service"]
